WEBVTT

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.620
Good morning, Mother!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.450
Good morning, Milady.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:22.480
Good morning.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.380
Good morning, Father.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.110
Sisters, you returned home?

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.950
I came because I wanted to talk to you about something.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.290
It's about...

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.470
Can't you do something about that outfit of yours already?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.080
What do you mean by "that outfit"?

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.350
Those garments which gentlemen should be wearing.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.160
It's a requirement for soldiers to wear this, though.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.530
At this rate, your heart and soul will become those of a man.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:58.900
Elice is just concerned what your fiancé might think if he sees you like that.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.930
There are no differences between men and women in the army-

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.740
How long do you plan on playing your army games?

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.580
The Malvin family prides itself on its military tradition,

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.400
so it is all but natural I hold a commission in the army.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.540
The war has come to a close for some time, Alice.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.710
The real struggle has just begun.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.480
Because of the war damages,

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.330
the land and the people living there are impoverished.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:24.090
The Imperial Army S.S. III brings relief to the land and-

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:24.540
That's enough about that cheery unit of yours.
The Imperial Army S.S. III brings relief to the land and-

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.490
That's enough about that cheery unit of yours.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.620
There are much more suitable posts for nobles.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.520
With all due respect, Father,

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.770
I take pride in myself from
Section III's mission of bringing war relief!

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.580
It has always been the duty of the nobility to safeguard and guide the people.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.240
I have taken the lead and immersed myself amongst the people...

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.100
...and have spared no effort in accomplishing that duty.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.040
We nobles should try to bring down
the barriers between us and the people.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.960
Bring down the barriers, eh?

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:57.750
Yes.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.510
What a shallow thought.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:03.600
Father?

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:04.870
I...

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:06.330
Look at the table.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:13.270
Hearing what you just said when you are being served bread every day in these impoverished times...

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.370
...that sounds even more shallow.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.910
What? The LT isn't here yet?

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.510
Yes.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.050
You're kidding me.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.550
I should've taken my time coming here then.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:35.760
Yeah, I'm sure you would've been able to take care of that kiss mark if you'd done that.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.990
But man, that stubborn head is actually late...

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.090
Rare things do happen.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.110
Well, maybe something happened.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:49.180
I'm worried!

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.030
The Lieutenant isn't a habitually late person like you, Oreld-san.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.940
Watch what you're saying!

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.940
Who are you calling a habitually late person?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.200
You little...

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.000
My apologies for being late!

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.490
Alice-san, what happened?

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.620
Did you run all the way from your house?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.130
Of course.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:12.160
Commoners do not have carriages that bring them to work and back home.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.360
Here, have a cup of water.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.670
Thank you.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.560
Do commoners drink water?

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.700
Of... Of course we do!

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:25.660
She's saying weird things again.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.100
This tastes delicious.
She's saying weird things again.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:27.300
I never thought water would be so delicious.
She's saying weird things again.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:27.520
I never thought water would be so delicious.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.680
Something must've happened to her.
I never thought water would be so delicious.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.710
My apologies for being late.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.580
We have a mission.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.390
The location is the southern part of the Empire - the Su-13 Tunnel.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.830
We've been asked to repair this tunnel after its collapse during the war.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.880
...we are part of the State Section, right?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:57.370
Yeah?

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.120
But now, they're telling us to drill a hole with this?

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.440
What's the meaning of all this?

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.400
Restoring the transportation system is crucial to the revival of the nation.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.480
In turn, the profit gained will benefit the country.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:08.630
Exactly!

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.460
The restoration of the rail tracks,

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.230
a very fitting job for Section III!

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:14.850
It's a good opportunity!

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:17.230
We'll be doing hard labor, too!

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:21.740
Aren't we supposed to tell the local contractors what to do?

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:24.820
No, if we can work with pickaxes together,

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.130
I'm sure we would be able to appreciate each other more.

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.030
That's what you think aswell, right, Corporal?

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.290
Y-Yeah...

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.190
Did you hear that?

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:38.360
N-No... I...

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.140
You didn't eat anything?

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.730
I ate a little...

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.030
I ate...

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.030
Are you fasting or something?

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:55.010
Can't we take care of all this with the shield train?

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.890
Just charge right in and...

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.030
It looks like it could collapse any moment.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.400
It will cave-in if we do anything reckless.

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:06.530
So we need to reinforce the sidewalls and the ceiling first...

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.500
Hold it right there, kiddo!

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.820
Quit squirming already!

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.490
Let go!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:12.660
What's the matter?
Let go!

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:13.070
What's the matter?

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.360
I said let me go!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.110
He appears to be from a nearby village.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.270
He was caught stealing some rations for our workers.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.080
It's only a little!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.100
The army gets all the good things to eat!

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.090
You little rascal, you scratched me!

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.910
Are you trying to inflict violence on civilians, huh?

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.060
Stop talking so arrogantly, you thief!

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:32.930
Wait.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:38.680
Eat it up properly.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.270
LT?

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:44.400
Neechan?

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:45.870
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.270
Could you take me to the leader of your village?

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:51.240
I would like to contract some workers for this construction.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:54.410
What's your name?

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:55.600
Peter.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.630
What about you, Neechan?

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:57.660
Alice.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.610
We refuse.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.500
Come on, Dad!

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:09.480
You said we needed work because we had a bad harvest!

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.260
No means no.

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:14.900
The opening of the tunnel should be profitable for this village, too!

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:15.860
Yet, why are you-

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:16.320
Five years ago...
Yet, why are you-

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:16.940
Five years ago...

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:19.900
This place was turned into a battlefield, too.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.700
The battle destroyed all the crops,

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:25.480
and the tunnel crumbled due to explosions.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.900
Then, just like today, we were commissioned for the restoration of the tunnel.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.080
Oh, we worked with all our hearts...

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:37.470
...because we were promised enough money for the village to prosper for a whole year.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.840
With that money, we wouldn't have to be hungry anymore.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:43.760
Finally, we finished the construction...

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.690
...while paying a dear price.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.770
We never got our money though.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.970
There was a loophole in the contract.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.320
The money meant to be our ray of hope...

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:01.340
...was replaced with the "privilege"
of being exempted from military draft.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.470
Oh, I am so thankful!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:10.420
Thanks to that, twelve from this village died from famine or disease instead of bullets that year.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.210
I won't let you say that's a small number.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.220
This kid is the only kid that's still alive from that.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.900
But, Alice isn't that kind of a person!

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:20.690
Quiet!

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.540
Don't be interfering with the problems of grown-ups, kid!

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:24.890
But Dad...

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.220
Apparently it crumbled again around the time of the ceasefire,

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.290
but that's none of our business.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.630
We're not going to work for nothing anymore.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:34.470
Things will be fine this time.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.940
The renumeration has been properly stated on the papers.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:37.980
When?

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:40.640
When are we getting paid?

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.620
Umm, it's...

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:45.180
...one month after construction has begun...

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.280
Forget it.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:47.890
I can't trust that at all.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.960
Yo, man...

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:50.400
Yeah?!

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.680
Couldn't you trust us?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.110
Oh, right! We'll work together with you!

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:58.120
We will eat the same things and work the same times.
Oh, right! We'll work together with you!

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.130
We will eat the same things and work the same times.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.080
We're prepared to go through
the same joy and pain as you all.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.630
Let the people and the army
join forces in times of hardships?

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.530
Out of the question.

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.170
Neechan.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.560
Is preaching those dreamy ideas all you can do?

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:19.180
This kid here can do the same thing.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.140
Go home.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:34.360
Ahh, we're not trusted at all.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.050
The gap between us is very large...

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.880
LT?

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.910
I must advance the construction progress even by a little.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:44.860
I understand how you feel,

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.690
but you won't accomplish anything by yourself.

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:49.100
Then you guys help me, too!

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.420
Shouldn't have said that...

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:53.920
This is all because of what you said, yo.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.630
Food is ready.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.630
I don't need any!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.150
You should eat something.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.340
Yeah, food, food.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:07.690
You know the saying
"can't fight a war on an empty stomach"-

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:08.290
You think I can eat?!
You know the saying
"can't fight a war on an empty stomach"-

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:09.520
You think I can eat?!

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.830
Especially after hearing their story?!

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:13.580
So, since this morning...

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:17.640
So many people are suffering from hunger...

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:22.030
...yet for the past eighteen years, I have taken my food for granted.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:23.910
I am a fool...

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:25.690
Lieutenant...

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.350
But still...

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:30.330
Wow, what's this machine?

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.080
Hey, kid!

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.960
Don't touch anything without our permission!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.090
Hey, pops!

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:35.590
Is this a tank?

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.200
Who are you calling "pops"?

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.100
Besides, it's all because of your dad that we're in trouble-

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.480
Don't blame it on the child!

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:43.520
LT...

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:47.020
Does this look like a tank, Peter?

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.460
Alice!

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:52.210
This thing is awesome!

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:53.120
A mega-drill!

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.670
It's called a shield train.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:57.950
It travels in front of the foot soldiers...

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.000
...and was developed to destroy barbed wire and sandbags.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.940
So, it's like a tank?

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:03.680
It's different.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.240
Right now, it's just a machine for drilling tunnels.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:10.390
It'll be a problem for you if the tunnel doesn't reopen, right?

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.150
Your superiors will scold you and...

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.240
Kids shouldn't worry about that.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:15.910
I'll be fine.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.380
Since you came all the way here, eat this before you go.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.730
But this is your lunch, right?

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:23.010
Don't worry; just eat it.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:26.870
Okay then... I'm digging in!

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.280
Yummy!

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.420
This is the first time I've eaten something this good!

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:33.750
That's nice.

00:12:34.030 --> 00:12:35.740
Alice, you're not hungry?

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:37.170
Don't worry about me.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.110
I ate enough...

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.780
Even when you guys were struck with hunger...

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:46.190
Alice, don't worry about what Dad said.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:49.280
The villagers didn't really care about that either,

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:53.070
but they just found a place to unload,

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:54.330
and that's why they were all worked up.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.750
No, your father was admirable.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.130
He can't say yes easily for the sake of the village.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:00.290
But-

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:05.130
Besides, it seems as though your father couldn't trust me more than the Empire.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.010
Alice!

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.200
Pardon me...

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.390
Let me be by myself...

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:16.580
Leave that over there when you're done eating, okay?

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:21.590
I'll help out if you guys need it!

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.100
Okay?!

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:30.010
I am a noble...

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.830
...but an inferior one!

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:35.300
I lived through my life ignorant...

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.020
...of the suffering of the people!

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:41.540
He must have seen that in me.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.040
I...

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.510
Grandfather, Grandfather!

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.750
What is it, Alice?

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:05.850
Don't you get lonely living in such
a big mansion by yourself, Grandfather?

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:11.530
But you're here right now.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.260
Besides...

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:14.800
What?

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:20.510
Nobles are all somewhat lonesome.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.030
Lonesome...

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.280
Why...?

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:33.780
I don't know.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.830
It seems like I...

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:40.740
...fell asleep...

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.420
...something soldiers should not...

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.780
Your dinner.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.430
I said I don't need it.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.590
Do you want to collapse again?

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:51.600
My determination is very strong-

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.120
Th-This is because you're showing it to me!

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.290
Take it away!

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.080
This country is wretched.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:02.650
Everyone is suffering from the disease known as "war damage".

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.860
"War damage" is the disease.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.720
"People" are the patients.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:15.510
I guess Section III plays the part of the "doctor".

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:20.430
Lieutenant.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:26.350
Do patients want doctors to endure the same disease as them?

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:33.870
Patients do not necessarily want others to understand their pain and suffering...

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.970
Nor do they want to be friends with the doctors.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:42.170
They just want to be saved; that's it.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.840
Even though that's kind of an empty way of thinking...

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.480
You know...

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.740
This smells good.

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:55.870
Please eat, then.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:06.030
Gathering us all together this early in the day...

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.650
I told you guys to go home!

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:10.810
What now?

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.010
You're gonna use force after we won't just do as you want?

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.110
Now we know your real intentions.

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:21.840
Although the handle makes it look like a military sword...

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.340
Behold!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.380
The Emperor's Seal that was bestowed upon me,

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:29.750
the treasured sword of the Malvin family, one of the Thirteen Appointed Families!

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.910
The proof of the next master of the family - "the Successor"!

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.920
The Thirteen Families?

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.560
Those special nobles that are allowed to attend the Imperial Assembly?

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.330
A young girl like her?

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.680
No matter how high of a person you are-

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:44.160
I swear an oath by this Successor.
No matter how high of a person you are-

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.980
I swear an oath by this Successor.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.260
The renumeration for your work five years ago and this time...

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:50.330
I swear I will make the army pay it to you,

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:52.740
even if it means putting my family's house up for auction!

00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:01.290
I don't like how you're wielding your authority,

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:06.740
but you seem more trustworthy than yesterday, at least.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:12.490
Then-

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:13.590
LT, we've got a problem!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.830
That kid got on the shield train by himself and...

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:20.620
Why didn't you stop him right away?!

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:24.430
Well, I heard a loud noise,
and when I woke up, the entrance was already...

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.690
I'll help out if you guys need it!

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:28.260
Peter...

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:32.650
Lieutenant, what are you doing?!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.920
I'm going to go in and stop the shield train.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.160
That's crazy!

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.500
You'll be buried alive!

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.450
He's my son!

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.080
I'm going!

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.220
Silence!

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.080
We are the Pumpkin Scissors!

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.300
This is our task!

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.040
Damn it!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.420
Whoa...

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.600
She's some woman...

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:52.840
That's a noble?

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:57.470
It's too dangerous!

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:59.030
Civilians must stay outside-

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:03.530
Didn't you say that the people and the army should join forces in times of hardships?

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.270
Hurry!

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:15.440
Peter!

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.390
Alice! Dad!

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:18.230
Are you all right?

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:19.640
Stop the engine now!

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:20.510
This place is going to collapse!

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:23.330
I... can't... move...

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:24.350
Peter!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.160
Watch out!

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:30.540
Are you all right?

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:31.950
Forget about me.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:33.010
Get my son!

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:47.830
The collapse stopped?

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:49.980
Alice...

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.700
Thank God, you're all right.

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:53.990
I'm... I'm sorry...

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:58.160
I... just... wanted to help you...

00:18:58.450 --> 00:18:59.650
Don't worry.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:01.170
Everything's okay now.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:03.050
You stupid kid.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.160
Dad!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.720
I've got bad news.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.300
I can't see sunlight anymore.

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:19.310
We're completely trapped inside.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:22.810
Can't we get him out at least?

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.070
Don't worry; my subordinates will come and get us out.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:27.950
That's some confidence you have in them.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:31.140
And you sure are an idiot.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:33.200
You're a very well-off person,

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.170
yet you're doing something that puts your life at risk.

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.140
It's precisely because I'm well-off...

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:41.400
...that I must throw away my life in certain situations, as well.

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:48.730
And I thought you nobles never treated us like humans even though you can say that whitewash.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.900
There was a cave-in incident five years ago also.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:58.230
They abandoned us back then and ran away.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.490
That's why I hate nobles.

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:04.960
I am sorry.

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:08.370
But if you weren't a noble,

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:10.850
you probably wouldn't have done something this stupid.

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:16.360
It's starting again...

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.470
Looks like we won't be saved in time.

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:20.990
No, they will come for us.

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:24.500
The time has come.

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:26.370
Careful!

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.200
Run!

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:38.470
A blue light?

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:40.930
It's him!

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:44.470
W-We're saved?

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:45.510
Yeah.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:47.320
There's nothing to worry about anymore.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:55.190
Oh, they're doing their job, all right.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:05.450
Although it may have been an accident,
it showed these people that the LT was serious.

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:09.610
Well, this is all thanks to us leaving our posts.

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:11.640
Weren't you sleeping?

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:13.500
We went on a little piss break.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:15.960
No wonder...

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:18.760
That was such a big mistake on my part...

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:20.610
Hey, the three of you over there!

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:23.350
Pick up your axes once you're done eating!

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.040
We shall be working together with them!

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.030
No, umm...

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:31.100
Shouldn't we just stand tall here?

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:34.030
Our prestige won't fall just because we're doing hard work!

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.310
Doesn't she seem energetic...

00:21:36.630 --> 00:21:37.420
Hurry up!

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:39.820
Soldiers should eat their meals as quickly as possible!

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:40.820
Yes, sir...

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.500
Did she stop fasting or something?

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:57.630
I will save this Empire from this disease called "war damage"!

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:34.430
Mer-kun, remember that tank
Section III confiscated last episode?

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:36.680
It looks like there's something special about that tank,

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:38.680
and something bad is about to happen.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:41.480
Next time, "The Deteriorating Portrait".

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:43.690
Come get us if you're not scared!
